# TypeScript Patterns

## Strict mode is on

`tsconfig.json` has `"strict": true`. This enables `strictNullChecks`, `noImplicitAny`, `strictFunctionTypes`, etc. All code must comply.

Do not use `as any` without a code comment explaining why it is unavoidable. Prefer narrowing with type guards or explicit interface casting.

```typescript
// Acceptable with justification
const agent = listing.agentId as unknown as PopulatedAgent; // populated by .populate()

// Not acceptable
const user = someValue as any;
```

## Enum pattern — as const objects only

Never use TypeScript `enum`. Use `as const` object pattern, which produces literal union types and works correctly with Mongoose and Zod.

```typescript
// Correct — used throughout this codebase
export const UserRole = {
  STUDENT: 'student',
  AGENT: 'agent',
  OWNER: 'owner',
  ADMIN: 'admin',
} as const;
export type UserRoleType = (typeof UserRole)[keyof typeof UserRole];

// Wrong — never use this
enum UserRole { STUDENT = 'student', AGENT = 'agent' }
```

Examples in codebase: `UserRole`, `PropertyType`, `ListingStatus`, `AvailabilityStatus`, `PaymentStatus`, `PaymentMethod`.

## Mongoose model export guard

Always use the hot-reload guard. In Next.js dev mode with Turbopack, modules can be re-evaluated, causing "Cannot overwrite model once compiled" errors.

```typescript
const User: IUserModel =
  (mongoose.models.User as IUserModel) ||
  mongoose.model<IUser, IUserModel>('User', UserSchema);

export default User;
```

## Mongoose document interfaces

Define a `Document` interface (`IUser`, `IListing`, etc.) and a `Model` interface (`IUserModel`, `IListingModel`) that extends `Model<I*>` with static methods. This is the pattern used in all models under `src/lib/db/models/`.

```typescript
export interface IListing extends Document {
  _id: mongoose.Types.ObjectId;
  title: string;
  // ...
  toPublicObject(): Partial<IListing>;
}

export interface IListingModel extends Model<IListing> {
  findActive(filter?: FilterQuery<IListing>): Promise<IListing[]>;
  findActiveById(id: string): Promise<IListing | null>;
}
```

## Service return types — explicit interfaces, not Mongoose documents

Service functions must return plain typed interfaces, not raw Mongoose documents. This prevents accidental access to private fields like `password`, `addressFull`, and `mapFull`.

```typescript
// Correct — service returns typed plain object
export async function createListing(agentId: string, data: CreateListingInput): Promise<PublicListing> {
  await connectDB();
  const listing = await Listing.create({ ...data, agentId });
  return toPublicListing(listing); // converts document to plain typed object
}

// Wrong — returning raw Mongoose document
export async function createListing(...): Promise<IListing> { ... }
```

Canonical return types: `PublicListing`, `UnlockedListing`, `ListingAgent`, `ListingAgentUnlocked` (listings service); `SessionUser` (auth).

## JWT payload type

Use `TokenPayload` from `src/lib/auth/jwt.ts` for all JWT-related types. It extends `JWTPayload` from `jose`.

```typescript
import type { TokenPayload } from '@/lib/auth/jwt';
```

The payload shape: `{ userId, email, role, type: 'access' | 'refresh' }`.

## API response types

- `ApiResponse<T>` from `src/lib/api/types.ts` — the canonical wire shape `{ success, data?, error?, errors? }`
- `SessionUser` from `src/lib/api/types.ts` — the canonical client-side user object

Do not use the `User` interface from `src/types/index.ts` in API hooks or API responses — that is an older shape used in some legacy UI components. New code uses `SessionUser`.

## AuthContext type

When writing or wrapping route handlers, use the `AuthContext` type from `src/lib/auth/guards.ts`:

```typescript
import type { AuthContext } from '@/lib/auth/guards';

export const POST = withAgent(async (request: NextRequest, context: AuthContext) => {
  const { userId, email, role } = context.user;
});
```

## Type utilities

- `cn(...classes)` from `src/lib/utils.ts` — Tailwind class merging (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`)
- `formatNaira(amount)` from `src/lib/utils/currency.ts` — Naira formatting
- `formatDate(date)` from `src/lib/utils/date.ts` — date formatting with `dayjs`

## Infer Zod types with z.infer

Always use `z.infer` to derive TypeScript types from Zod schemas:

```typescript
export const createListingSchema = z.object({ ... });
export type CreateListingInput = z.infer<typeof createListingSchema>;
```

This is the pattern in all `src/lib/validators/` files.

## Mongoose ObjectId handling

When comparing ObjectIds, always `.toString()`:

```typescript
if (listing.agentId.toString() !== agentId) {
  throw new Error('You do not have permission to update this listing');
}
```

When creating ObjectIds from strings:

```typescript
new mongoose.Types.ObjectId(someStringId)
```

